{
 "doc": "Item 11.10: face masking and retained information. Evaluates the embeddings extracted by w2_embed.py (box) from the\nlocked MEVID test frames (four frames per tracklet) under mask variants, for the two retrained encoders.\n\nPRE-REGISTERED BEFORE THE FIRST EXTRACTION (2026-10-07, wave 2). The privacy claim this evidence may support is\nonly: 'retrieval accuracy and cross-camera linkability of appearance embeddings after face-region masking, and which\nnon-face information the embedding still carries'. It cannot support 'privacy protection', since linkability is\nexactly what the retrieval task measures.\n  Variants: none (positive control), yunet (OpenCV YuNet face boxes, score >= 0.6, expanded 30 percent, filled with the\n  frame mean colour), band_top15 / band_top25 (top 15 / 25 percent of rows filled; detector-free head region),\n  band_mid15 / band_mid25 (equal-area control bands at rows 45-60 / 35-60 percent).\n  H1 (positive control): variant none equals the cached embeddings exactly (max abs difference 0.0).\n  H2 (linkability survives masking): for yunet and band_top25, general-protocol mAP retains at least 80 percent of the\n     unmasked value (identity-cluster 95 percent CI of the ratio of means has lower limit >= 0.80). FALSIFIED otherwise.\n  H3 (the head band is not special): the mAP change from band_top25 minus the change from the equal-area control\n     band_mid25 has an identity-cluster CI that includes 0. A CI below 0 would indicate head-region reliance.\n  H4 (detector coverage, descriptive): share of frames with a detected face, and of detected face centres that lie\n     inside the top 25 percent band; the detector is not validated on this data, so a non-detection is not evidence of\n     absence of face pixels.\n  Retained information (cache based): ridge-regression probe of the camera id from the embedding, identity-grouped\n  5-fold cross-validation (the probe never sees the held-out identity), against the majority-class rate.\nMultiplicity: Holm over the paired mAP tests (variants x protocols x seeds).\nusage: python3 -I w2_facemask_eval.py PULLED_DIR   (PULLED_DIR holds test_<variant>_<seed>.npz from the box)\nOutputs results/w2_facemask.json.\n",
